ArcErc8183Fork
├── deployment
│   ├── when the Arc chain ID differs
│   │   └── it should fail the pinned deployment test
│   ├── when the proxy implementation differs
│   │   └── it should fail the pinned deployment test
│   └── when the payment token differs
│       └── it should fail the pinned deployment test
├── setBudget
│   ├── when the caller is the client
│   │   └── it should revert Unauthorized
│   └── when the caller is the provider
│       └── it should record the fuzzed USDC budget
├── submit
│   ├── when the caller is not the provider
│   │   └── it should revert Unauthorized
│   └── when the funded provider submits
│       └── it should transition Funded to Submitted
├── complete
│   ├── when the caller is not the evaluator
│   │   └── it should revert Unauthorized
│   └── when the evaluator completes a submitted job
│       ├── it should transition Submitted to Completed
│       └── it should conserve client, escrow, provider, evaluator, and treasury USDC
└── claimRefund
    ├── when the job has not expired
    │   └── it should revert WrongStatus
    └── when any caller claims after expiry
        ├── it should return the full budget only to the client
        └── it should transition Funded to Expired

Test boundary
├── deployment and ABI assertions read the real Arc Testnet fork
└── state-changing USDC tests replace only Arc USDC bytecode with a test ERC-20
    └── because Arc native USDC delegates transfers to a chain-specific system contract unsupported by vanilla Foundry

ArcErc8183Invariant
├── while the job is Funded or Submitted
│   └── escrow should retain exactly the job budget above its fork baseline
├── after Completed, Rejected, or Expired
│   └── escrow should return to its fork baseline
└── after every generated action sequence
    └── tracked USDC should be conserved
